rk3588-camera-overlays (0.2.0-1) UNRELEASED; urgency=medium

  * Split camera overlays the way the Raspberry Pi does: one dtbo per
    board CSI port, and one dtbo per sensor (imx708, imx219, imx519).
    Select a camera with imx708,port0. 4lane, link-frequency, rotation,
    and orientation are baked in by apply-overlays.sh.
  * The first camera in overlays.conf enables isp0 and the second isp1.
    isp0 or isp1 on a camera overrides that. Port overlays no longer
    pick an ISP.
  * unite on one camera enables the dual-ISP device (both register
    windows and both IOMMUs) and rejects a second camera.

 -- Peyton Howe <peyton@localhost>  Sun, 18 Oct 2026 12:00:00 +0000

rk3588-camera-overlays (0.1.2-1) UNRELEASED; urgency=medium

  * apply-overlays.sh treats overlays.conf as the full camera-overlay list:
    it replaces previously managed camera/ISP entries in U_BOOT_FDT_OVERLAYS
    and keeps unrelated overlays. Clearing the conf removes camera overlays.

 -- Peyton Howe <peyton@localhost>  Tue, 29 Sep 2026 12:00:00 +0000

rk3588-camera-overlays (0.1.1-1) UNRELEASED; urgency=medium

  * Add rk3588-isp.dtbo (ISP nodes from kernel patch 0002) and have
    apply-overlays.sh apply it before the camera overlays, so they work on
    stock DTBs that have __symbols__ but no ISP nodes (e.g. ROCK 5B+).
  * ROCK 5B+ cam1 (VICAP variant) now enables isp1, so it gets rkisp2
    processing and can run alongside cam0 on isp0.

 -- Peyton Howe <peyton@localhost>  Tue, 29 Sep 2026 12:00:00 +0000

